Description: July — a Bangla input method for Linux (Bornona layout)
 July is a Bangla input method for Linux built on IBus. It ships the
 fixed-layout Bornona keyboard mapping, with a draggable, edge-snapping
 floating mode-toggle bar in the spirit of Avro Keyboard, including a
 bilingual (বাংলা/English) in-bar user guide to the key mapping.
 .
 After install, the floating bar autostarts for all users and makes
 the Bornona engine active automatically. On some desktops (those
 without ibus already configured as the input method framework) you may
 need to run "im-config -n ibus" once and log back in.
